{"repositoryId":891000278,"availability":"available","full":"with-ours/ours-vite-react-router","name":"ours-vite-react-router","description":"This repository provides an example of integrating Ours analytics with a Vite + React Router application. It demonstrates how to set up the Ours pixel script, track page views on route changes, and log custom events, all while maintaining HIPAA-compliant analytics for privacy-focused applications.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2024-11-19T14:54:51Z","updated":"2026-10-12T21:31:05Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://docs.oursprivacy.com/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:05.024Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:05.024Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T07:38:05.024Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T07:38:05.024Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This repo is a working reference for integrating the Ours Privacy CDP (Customer Data Platform) and CMP (Consent Management Platform) into a client-side React application using Vite and React Router. Browse the code to see how each product is installed, initialized, and used.","In a client-side React SPA, index.html is the single entry point for every route. It is the right place to load analytics and consent scripts because:"],"features":["It runs once — the HTML loads when the visitor first arrives. Scripts initialize once and persist across client-side route navigations.","It covers every page — every route the React Router renders inherits whatever is in index.html, with no extra configuration.","Load order is deterministic — scripts in execute in document order, so placing the CMP before the CDP guarantees consent is available before tracking starts."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/with-ours/ours-vite-react-router/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3861a5a749e980a39c57d7a36085b66772ebadda0137e1fe568c3297d38a44